      "distance": "22,6 km",
      "time": "6 hours 28 min",
      "short_desc": "Final week on the Camin. Pilgrim Rush, Drizzle & a Swedish Encounter",
      "long_desc": " We left Sarria around 9 AM and immediately noticed the stream of people heading out, like a pilgrim parade. Many are new walkers starting their Camino here in Sarria, just covering the final 100 km required to receive the Compostela in Santiago. A few kilometers in, we were caught up by a Swedish couple from Örebro. We had previously connected through the “Swedish Pilgrims” Facebook group, so the meeting was unexpected but familiar. Around the 7–8 km mark, we stopped at a small café for a well-deserved break, coffee and a fresh juice to recharge. The weather was mixed throughout the day, with light rain on and off, but it didn’t dampen the spirit. Once in Portomarín, we checked into Hotel Portomarin Star for the night. We wrapped up the day with a delicious dinner at Restaurante Mirador, overlooking the town. A great end to a peaceful and slightly rainy walking day.",
