    {
      "week": 7,
      "day": 44,
      "title": "Portomarín -> Ligonde (Airexe)",
      "distance": "18,0 km",
      "time": "5 hours 34 min",
      "short_desc": "Still raining. Familiar faces, school pilgrims and heavy Galician rain",
      "long_desc": "We started walking from Portomarín at first light, enjoying a dry and mild morning, no need for jackets or rain gear, for once. At breakfast, we met Sandra and Susie from San Diego again, familiar faces we’ve crossed paths with several times now. The trail led us through the beautiful Galician countryside, and soon we encountered a group of high school students from Madrid walking the Camino with their class. They’re spending five days on the trail, staying in albergues and cooking their own meals, a wonderful way to build camaraderie and experience the Camino early in life.Great Spanish tradition. Since Sarria, we’ve noticed a big improvement in the availability and quality of cafés and restaurants. Galicia truly stands out, not just for its lush landscapes, but also for its flavorful food compared to Castilla y León. Later in the afternoon, we bumped into Nancy and Dave from Fort Lauderdale, whom we first met in Ponferrada. They had just started walking then and are scheduled to finish the day after us. Coincidentally, we’ll also be staying at the same hotel in Santiago! Just before reaching our accommodation, Casa de Cota in Airexe, the skies opened up and we were hit with a heavy downpour, a classic welcome from rainy Galicia.",
